  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.0\n - First Visualizer - Charts.Pie\nv1.0.1\n - Upgraded SetValues from using float to double for Current and Max, and Multiplier Values; Old internal Pie Region Disposal can now be toggled by setting true to \"EnableInternalDisposal\".\n - Calculates Inner Radius on the constructor instead of the SetValues Method.\n - Added \"EnableInternalDisposal\" to dispose Region created previously by the Pie.SetValues method.\n - Naming corrections. Now called \"Diameter\" instead of \"Radius\" to correctly reflect with the behavior.\n - Implemented some internal value clamps, and re-evaluated calculations to match some parts of the Pie Code.\nV1.0.2\n - Added a Size variant for creating Pie.\n - Pie chart now centers with the actual element region. No longer fixed to top-left.\nV1.0.3\n - QUICK PATCH: Renamed \"Create\" to \"CreateWithSize\" for the initializer that requires Size instead of int for pie.",
